# Rule Source Hierarchy (Conflict Resolution)

    1. `.clinerules` (this file) — AUTHORITATIVE. All other rule sources defer to this file.
    2. `.cursorrules` — Cursor IDE-specific subset. If any rule conflicts with `.clinerules`, `.clinerules` wins with no debate.
    3. System environment_details — Operational context only. Does not override architectural constraints.

    When the LLM detects a contradiction between `.clinerules` and `.cursorrules`, it MUST:
        - Log the conflict internally (do not output to user)
        - Apply the `.clinerules` version
        - Flag `.cursorrules` as stale/requiring synchronisation

